    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "21b37a971e41a77b16baf8320d52700f8ed11716f543cf34c3abf8caf0737505",
      "text": "After breakfast, transfer to the airport for your flight to Foz do Iguaçu, where you are welcomed and taken to your hotel. Then set off on a tour of the falls. On the border of Brazil, Argentina and Paraguay, within a national park of unique flora and fauna, 275 waterfalls, each with its own name, crash into the canyon of the Devil’s Throat; their name means “big water” in Guarani. The contrast between the calm, almost lazy river above the falls and the boiling torrents plunging into the gorge below is stunning: you could watch this spectacle for hours.\n\nOptional, at an additional cost: the Macuco Safari and the Bird Park (see Optional excursions).\n\nNot included: Flight Rio de Janeiro – Foz do Iguaçu\n\n**Helicopter flight over Iguazu Falls**\n\nOptional, at an additional cost.\n\nFlight duration is around 10 minutes. Price to be confirmed.\n\nAfter the programme, return to the hotel.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw38xoel-amanda",
        "model": "GPT-6",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The Word 2027 Brazilian-side programme is used verbatim for the core day, optional Macuco Safari/Bird Park and excluded flight. Word contains no helicopter excursion, ten-minute flight duration, pending quote or final return sentence; these absent assigned RU details are translated and appended. Macuco remains optional as explicitly specified by Word.",
        "wordVerified": {
          "fileId": "1uABQ0zRQzYr2BAfQJdxCiSzAnVokBp8V",
